  "final_answer": "Based on the analysis of the frontend codebase, deleting the backend endpoint `POST /api/ai/chats` is a **BREAKING** change. \n\nHere are the details of the TypeScript consumers that will break:\n\n### 1. **Service Class**\n* **File:** `ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/ai-chat.service.ts`\n* **Method:** `createChat(chat: ChatConfiguration, config?: RequestConfig)`\n* **Code Reference:**\n  ```typescript\n  public createChat(chat: ChatConfiguration, config?: RequestConfig): Observable<string> {\n    return this.http.post<string>(`/api/ai/chats`, chat, defaultHttpOptionsFromConfig(config));\n  }\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Component Class (UI Consumer)**\n* **File:** `ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/components/ai/ai-assistant-panel.component.ts`\n* **Method:** `sendMessage(prompt: AiPromptMessage)`\n* **Impact:** When a user starts a new chat and sends their first message, the component relies on `this.aiChat.createChat` to initialize the conversation and retrieve a `chatId`. Deleting this endpoint will prevent users from starting new AI Assistant chats.\n* **Code Reference:**\n  ```typescript\n  const startOrContinue$ = this.chatId()\n    ? of(null)\n    : this.aiChat.createChat({title: 'New chat'}, {ignoreLoading: true, ignoreErrors: true}).pipe(\n      tap(chatId => {\n        this.isCreatingNew.set(false);\n        this.chatId.set(chatId);\n        this.panelService.setLastChatId(chatId);\n        this.panelService.addChat({id: chatId, title: 'New chat', createdTime: Date.now()});\n      })\n    );\n  ```",
